  <section class="hidden" aria-hidden="true">
    <h2>Target score</h2>
    <div class="empty-note">Score doesn't depend on which mock's population you happened to be compared against — it's just marks earned (+3 correct, −1 wrong), so it's the steadiest thing to track session to session. This is your primary target. Percentile below is a softer, secondary read — worth glancing at, not the thing to optimize.</div>
    <div class="field" style="margin-top:12px;">
      <label for="targetScoreLegacy">Overall score you're aiming for</label>
      <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" id="targetScoreLegacy" min="0" step="1" placeholder="e.g. 110">
